    <string name="help_1_text">Open a recording, or record with the microphone. Say what it is, and Brasscribe writes down the notes and arranges them for brass band.</string>
    <string name="help_2_title">The “?” marks</string>
    <string name="help_2_text">A “?” above a note means Brasscribe wasn\'t sure. A boxed “?” means very unsure. Listen to the bar, then keep the note or change it.</string>
    <string name="help_3_title">Practise</string>
    <string name="help_3_text">Slow the music down with Speed, repeat the hard bars, and mute your part to play along with the band.</string>
    <string name="help_4_title">Share or print</string>
    <string name="help_4_text">Print your own part, every part for the band, or the conductor\'s score.</string>
    <string name="help_5_title">A whole band needs your computer</string>
    <string name="help_5_text">One instrument can be written down on the phone. For a full band, open Brasscribe on your computer and connect in Settings.</string>
    <string name="help_6_title">Links and streaming apps</string>
    <string name="help_6_text">Links can\'t be downloaded, and streaming apps usually block recording. A file you own, or the microphone, always works.</string>
